ted_at":"2026-02-16T21:14:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T18:37:38Z","closed_at":"2026-02-17T15:35:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116376","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116376","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116376.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116376.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-17T15:35:24Z"},"body":"Fixes #116304.\r\nFollow up to #114082.\r\n\r\n`DisplayServer::window_set_size` is called lots of times in the code, with the assumption (I suppose) that it's going to be idempotent.\r\n\r\nWe had checks in `_update_window_rect` but we still called `WaylandThread::window_set_size`, which did a lot of stuff. In particular, this caused issues with HiDPI as it \"overrode\" the window size before it had a time to figure out its scale.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTested on:\r\n - Fedora 43 VM with COSMIC 1.0.1, GNOME 49.2, KDE 6.5.4\r\n - KISS Linux with labwc 0.9.3-49-g654da8c8 (built from git), sway 1.11.\r\n\r\nBoth with and without #116308.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_even